    <statement><p>Find a vector parametrization of the circle of radius
<m>3</m> in the xy-plane, centered at the origin,
oriented clockwise so that the point <m>(3,0)</m> 
corresponds to <m>t = 0</m> and the point <m>(0,-3)</m>
corresponds to <m>t = 1</m>.</p>
<p><m>\vec{r}(t) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;3\cos\mathopen{}\left(\frac{\pi t}{2}\right),-3\sin\mathopen{}\left(\frac{\pi t}{2}\right)\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
